{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And whatever the unclean one touches shall be unclean.</b> The verse speaks of contact-impurity (tum'at ḥiburin) — meaning, while he is still attached to the corpse, he contracts seven-day impurity." "<b>And the person who touches.</b> Not through attachment — <b>until evening</b> shall he be unclean. Thus our Rabbis expounded. And according to the plain sense: <b>whatever the unclean one touches</b> — with food-impurity, whether utensils — and you have in it only evening-impurity. <b>And the person who touches</b> — this is an explanation of ״and he shall be unclean,״ to say that the time of his impurity is until evening."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:44.938621809Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}